<title>MONACO: TENNIS-LEADING ATP TOUR PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LEADING ATP TOUR PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading prize-money winners issued</p>
<p>by the ATP Tour on Tuesday:</p>
<p> 1. Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)	$2,235,448</p>
<p> 2. Pete Sampras (U.S.)		   1,946,252</p>
<p> 3. Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia)	  1,665,485</p>
<p> 4. Thomas Muster (Austria)	     1,545,496</p>
<p> 5. Michael Chang (U.S.)		  1,502,366</p>
<p> 6. Richard Krajicek (Netherlands)    1,231,761</p>
<p> 7. Boris Becker (Germany)		1,198,007</p>
<p> 8. Thomas Enqvist (Sweden)	     1,128,547</p>
<p> 9. Andre Agassi (U.S.)		   1,116,595</p>
<p> 10. Todd Woodbridge (Australia)	  998,133</p>
<p> 11. Mark Woodforde (Australia)	   987,027</p>
<p> 12. Wayne Ferreira (South Africa)	961,020</p>
<p> 13. Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands)	  946,586</p>
<p> 14. Marc Rosset (Switzerland)	    903,439</p>
<p> 15. Todd Martin (U.S.)		     868,636</p>
<p> 16. Jakob Hlasek (Switzerland)	   838,383</p>
<p> 17. Marcelo Rios (Chile)		   825,678</p>
<p> 18. Alberto Costa (Spain)		  793,741</p>
<p> 19. Jan Siemerink (Netherlands)	  753,881</p>
<p> 20. Petr Korda (Czech Republic)	  751,361</p>
</text>
